@startuml
title Opening the app and signing in
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #93C5FD
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
participant "Provider / screen" as UI
participant "Auth controller" as Auth
database "Storage adapter" as Storage
participant Backend
participant "Session store" as Store
UI -> Auth : restoreSession()
Auth -> Store : restoring()
Auth -> Storage : Check pending marker\nand native refresh token
alt Pending logout OR missing native refresh token
  Auth -> Store : clear() -> Anonymous
else May attempt restoration
  Auth -> Backend : Refresh (native token / web cookie)
  alt Refresh succeeds
    Backend --> Auth : Session data
    Auth -> Storage : Save rotated native refresh token, if present
    Auth -> Store : commit() -> Authenticated
  else Refresh rejected (401) or response malformed
    Auth -> Store : clear() -> Anonymous
    Auth -> Storage : Mark pending; delete native credential
  else Temporary refresh failure
    Auth -> Store : restoreFailed() if generation still current
    note over UI,Store : Session gate shows an error and retry button.
  end
end
opt User explicitly signs in
  UI -> Auth : signIn(email, password)
  Auth -> Store : clear(); remember generation
  Auth -> Backend : Login
  Backend --> Auth : Successful session response
  Auth -> Storage : Save native refresh token, if present\nClear pending marker
  Auth -> Store : commit() if generation still current
  Store --> UI : Notify subscribers -> authenticated UI
end
note over Auth,Backend
Auth operations are serialized.
Diagram assumes API URL is configured.
end note
@enduml
